(PRC-78 — `Shutdown.` performs reboot(2) with LINUX_REBOOT_CMD_POWER_OFF
 and needs CAP_SYS_BOOT.
 Also covers: PRC-79 (`Reboot.`), PRC-80 (`Halt.`), PRC-81 (`Poweroff` is
 an alias for Shutdown), PRC-82 (`Restart` is an alias for Reboot) and
 PRC-86 (on failure the error flag is set instead of crashing or exiting,
 `On error` catches it, and execution continues).
 SAFETY, read this before running it: this probe really does issue five
 reboot(2) calls. It is safe ONLY because the process is unprivileged --
 uid 1000 with an empty effective capability set, so every call returns
 EPERM before the kernel does anything. Run as root, or with CAP_SYS_BOOT,
 it powers the machine off at the first line. Check with `id` and
 `grep CapEff /proc/self/status` (0000000000000000) before running it.
 PRC-85 (on success none of these return) and PRC-84 (each calls sync(2)
 first) are NOT verified here and cannot be without taking the machine
 down.
 Ran, from the repo root, as uid 1000 with CapEff 0000000000000000:
   VOX_CORE_PATH=/home/josj/scr/english/vox/coreasm \
   /home/josj/scr/english/vox/target/release/vox \
   docs/ledger/probes/process-control/PRC-78.vox -o p && ./p
 expected output:
   Shutdown set the error flag
   Poweroff set the error flag
   Reboot set the error flag
   Restart set the error flag
   Halt set the error flag
   the machine is still here and execution continued
)
Shutdown.
On error print "Shutdown set the error flag".
Poweroff.
On error print "Poweroff set the error flag".
Reboot.
On error print "Reboot set the error flag".
Restart.
On error print "Restart set the error flag".
Halt.
On error print "Halt set the error flag".
print "the machine is still here and execution continued".
